\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {IV.3}{\ignorespaces Evolution of the activation fraction of three INAS parametrisations, against temperature and particle radius in semi-logarithmic scale. The $\gamma $ factor is not yet applied here, so all reach \SI {100}{\percent } activation. The slope of the threshold lines accounts for the relative weight of particle radius and temperature for the activation fraction. The saturated darker zones show the parameter space for which the parametrisations predict between \SI {10}{\percent } and full activation. Panel A is H18B (bacteria), B is M18 (sea sprays) and C is N12 (dust).}}{123}{figure.caption.78}\protected@file@percent }
